        "timestamp": 1779275808,
        "contenuto_esteso": "To display this content from YouTube, you must enable advertisement tracking and audience measurement. One of your browser extensions seems to be blocking the video player from loading. To watch this content, you may need to disable it on this site. Beijing as centre stage: Trump & Putin mark 'series of diplomatic visits to the court of Xi Jinping' Asia / Pacific Issued on: 20/05/2026 - 13:16 Genie Godula is pleased to welcome Dr. Flavia Lucenti, Postdoctoral Researcher at LUISS University for the EU Horizon Project REMIT. With Vladimir Putin in Beijing less than a week after Donald Trump’s own visit to China, Dr. Lucent emphasizes the historic significance in the sequencing of visits, revealing China’s increasingly central diplomatic role. She explores how the wars in Ukraine and Iran are reshaping the Sino Russian partnership. And Dr. Lucenti also highlights the structural asymmetry in the relationship: while China purchases a substantial share of Russian exports, “Russia accounts only 4% of China international trade”. Xi and Putin - Leaders praise 'unshakable foundations' at Beijing talks 20/05/2026 Asia / Pacific 'Crony capitalism and oligarchy': 'Remarkable correlation' between Adani's rise & Modi’s ascendancy 20/05/2026 Asia / Pacific 'Russia and China share same goal in constructing alternative world order', analyst says 19/05/2026 Asia / Pacific Putin lands in China for trip that aims to show unshakeable ties after Trump pomp 19/05/2026 Asia / Pacific China in a stronger position with US and Russia \"embroiled in wars they started\" 19/05/2026 Asia / Pacific How dependent is Russia on its economic ties with China? 19/05/2026 Asia / Pacific China projects itself as a \"stable power\" as it greets US and Russia in less than a week 19/05/2026 Asia / Pacific Russia-China trade set to dominate talks between two leaders 19/05/2026 Asia / Pacific What will Russia and China's leaders discuss over two-day visit? 19/05/2026 Asia / Pacific"
